    "title": "Salon Retail Margin: What Each Product Sale Leaves You",
    "seoTitle": "Salon Retail Product Profit Margin",
    "description": "Calculate salon retail margin after product cost, fees, commission and losses. Translate retail sales into appointment contribution and check stock cash.",
    "metaDescription": "Calculate salon retail margin after product cost, fees, commission and losses. Translate retail sales into appointment contribution and check stock cash.",
    "image": "/images/blog/salon-retail-product-profit-margin-editorial.webp",
    "alt": "Muted haircare bottles on a wooden salon shelf, with additional stock in a carton below.",
    "imageCaption": "Generated editorial image illustrating the work discussed in this guide; not a photograph of a real customer or business.",
    "published": "2026-10-05",
    "modified": "2026-10-05",
    "opening": "Sell a product for $30 after paying $12 to get it onto the shelf, and its product gross margin is 60%. After the example's commission, payment fee, packaging and stock losses, the sale leaves $13.10 toward the salon's monthly costs.",
    "unit": "appointments",
